      "title": "Fixed roles / first frame + persona + reel",
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "ver": "0.38.1",
        "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions: <Subject 1> is the original main person to be replaced in <Video 1>. <Subject 2> is the adult AI persona shown in BOTH <Picture 1> and <Picture 2>. <Picture 1> is the reconstructed opening frame of the source segment: the persona already occupies the source person's position, in the source scene and clothing. It is supplied as both a reference image and a frame-zero guide. <Picture 2> is a clear face reference of the same persona, not a different character or frame anchor. <Video 1> supplies the source performance and shot structure. <Audio 1> is its original soundtrack.\n\nretention_analysis: Preserve the opening composition and target person's appearance from <Picture 1>, with consistent facial identity supported by <Picture 2>. Transfer the original performer's action, pose changes, expressions, gaze, interactions and timing from <Video 1> to <Subject 2>. Preserve the source environment, clothing, props, camera and other people's roles. Keep the persona's own facial structure, hair and body proportions as she moves.\n\nrecreation_rules: The opening shot begins from the prepared scene in <Picture 1>. Continue with the source action rather than introducing the portrait's background, outfit or pose. The persona remains the same person during head turns, expression changes and occlusions. The original performer's facial features are not the target identity. Follow the source shot boundaries and local action timing described below.\n\naudio_roles: Follow the original speaking turns in <Audio 1>. The persona speaks only the replaced person's lines. Other visible or off-camera speakers keep their own roles, while the persona follows the source listening reactions. The original audio recording, including all voices and ambience, is exported directly. No voice conversion is performed."
      ],
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
